# ==============================================================================
# Build context for backend/Dockerfile and frontend/Dockerfile is the REPO ROOT:
#   docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .
#   docker build -f frontend/Dockerfile --build-arg NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=... .
#
# This is the only ignore file. A <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to a
# Dockerfile would silently take precedence over this one, so none exist.
#
# Never ignore what the Dockerfiles COPY:
#   package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml
#   backend/package.json, backend/tsconfig.json, backend/tsconfig.build.json,
#   backend/prisma.config.ts,
#   backend/prisma/, backend/app/, backend/docker-entrypoint.sh
#   frontend/ (whole package, minus the rebuilt or secret paths below)
# ==============================================================================

# Repository metadata and tooling
.git
.claude
.github
.husky
scripts
docker-compose.yml

# Not part of any image
docs
hack
e2e
deployment
design

# Dependencies (installed in the image from the lockfile)
**/node_modules

# Secrets: every .env variant, in every package
**/.env
**/.env.*
backend/.env
frontend/.env*

# Build outputs, caches, runtime data (rebuilt or mounted)
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/coverage
**/logs
**/uploads
**/*.log
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/generated

# Tests are not compiled into the images (tsconfig excludes them as well)
**/_tests_
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx

# Docker files themselves (the Dockerfile is passed with -f)
**/Dockerfile*
**/.dockerignore

# Documentation and editor files
**/*.md
# ... but the prompts are application data, not documentation: every text that
# goes to a model lives there and is loaded at runtime (CLAUDE.md).
!prompts/**
# ... and so is the corpus. Three of those four files are markdown, and without
# this line the image carries the PDF alone: the seed then fails on file two,
# inside the container, where the demo notebook is supposed to be created
# (M8-T1). Every image since M2-T5 was built that way; the first run of
# `docker compose exec backend node dist/prisma/seed.js` found it.
!backend/evals/corpus/**
**/.DS_Store
**/.editorconfig
